From ff8e1d0cee0f32f98b53fe9c970e6d70636319d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:29:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): carry creator decision asks to remote origin
 chats [daveey]

Problem: accepted worker-1 -> hub origin binding did not provide a decision
wake. Read-only SSM readback of t_eeeeee0000000017 confirms origin event
<origin-event-id>, chat refusal reported in comment<refusal-id>, successful HUMAN block
<blocked-event-id> at an example block time, and external scheduled event<park-id> at an example park time.
The latter waited on own comment<question-id>; creator answer<reply-id> is at an example reply time.
This corrects the incident premise: human_request itself was not refused.
No original/ASG card was changed.

Why 1: no creator turn consumed the second question -- it was an external
park, not a decision_requested event (authoritative worker event<park-id>).
Why 2: chat waits explicitly excluded platform=hub, so the worker's prior
chat park failed no_chat_subscriber despite its accepted origin binding
(kanban_awaiting.has_chat_subscriber; comment<refusal-id>).
Why 3: remote notice candidates, indexes, state and sweep gates handled
terminal cards, not scheduled decision envelopes; admitting hub rows alone
would leave the transport broken (remote_index_projection, remote
observations, unloaded gates, remote notices).
Why 4: adoption validates binding/link and publication ownership; its
handoff_complete receipt is not an end-to-end decision-delivery capability
receipt (kanban_origin_creation / kanban_origin_ledger). It truthfully
reported a bound link while the separate decision route remained absent.
Root (happened): current owner asks had no snapshot/consumer contract,
and own-card reply probes could silently be classified as external.
Root (not caught): local chat-wait tests deliberately enshrined hub
rejection; no adoption -> park -> owner snapshot -> remote wake regression.
Recurrence: local-orchestrator incident t_eeeeee0000000010 and the existing
chat-wait fixes (b31fffd8cb, 4e084ff899) cover local delivery/retry, not this
cross-gateway composition.

Countermeasures:
- Publish a validated current ask with owner snapshots, using event time
  and identity; do not resurrect an old ask after a later non-chat park.
- Include decisions throughout remote indexing/observations and host wake
  gates, and keep retrying when no agent wake can start (no passive ack).
- Treat self wait-comment probes as creator questions with normal
  subscriber/authority checks, even when tagged external/inferred.
- Explicitly address the creator agent; preserve genuine human-request
  rendering, human-block wake policy, approval authority and escalation.
- Composed adoption regression covers explicit creator, inferred/external
  reply probe, block(kind=time), and existing human_request transport.
  Fresh baseline replay: 4 creator variants fail; human characterization
  already passes. Also test budget retry, durable dedup, repeated/stale
  asks and malformed envelopes.

Validation: full scripts/check --base origin/main passes. Focused suite
and complete direct-consumer tests recorded on task t_eeeeee000000001c.
Installed/live scratch proof remains a post-landing acceptance step;
unit-test success is not a claim of deployment or natural wake.
